  "Id": 3101,
  "Title": "Economics of brain health",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Understanding the impact of a declining economy on health outcomes of children and young adults in South Africa",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In the last decade, we have seen massive contestation over the scope and nature of economic decline and how this phenomenon impacts brain health. Flawed economic advisers were offered to most governments as some economists supported austerity policies rejecting the evidence that economic decline harms brain health. Sadly, this costly mistake has led some economists to perceive austerity and economic decline as a tool to shrink the social welfare role of the state, setting in the wave of mental ill-health."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The most marginalized groups feel the biggest impacts of these economic injustices. For example, in the 1980s, austerity and economic decline led to increases in mortalities in Latin America and Africa as per capita growth turned negative. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Why austerity measures are still allowed to be implemented today is troubling-to say the least. The social costs of austerity and economic decline are enormous and undermine the brain health agenda. For example, following the implementation of austerity in the wake of the Eurozone crisis in Greece, cases of HIV infection worsened by 52% when the Greek government cut its budget for a needle-exchange program targeting drug addicts. Suicides spiked by 36% as mental health outcomes deteriorated. In Ireland, Portugal, and Spain, austerity and economic decline led to a massive increase in unemployment and wage stagnation. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Recently - our BMI Economist Prof Cyprian Mostert in a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "paper",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352827323000691",
                  "target": "_self",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " titled 'Macroeconomics and health: Understanding the impact of a declining economy on health outcomes of children and young adults in South Africa' discovered that economic decline in South Africa leads to worsening mental health and non-communicable diseases. Alcohol abuse drives the worsening of these conditions. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The study focused on children and young adults, a group that is particularly vulnerable to the effects of economic downturns. He found that a decline in the economy was associated with an increase in mortality rates among children under the age of five. Specifically, that for every 1% decrease in economic growth, there was a 0.6% increase in mortality rates among this age group."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "He suggests that these findings highlight the importance of policies that support economic growth and development, particularly in countries like South Africa where the health outcomes of children and young adults are already precarious. He notes that policies aimed at reducing poverty and inequality, improving access to healthcare, and promoting education and employment opportunities could have a significant impact on improving health outcomes in these vulnerable populations."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Overall, this study provides important insights into the complex relationship between macroeconomics and health. It highlights the need for policymakers to consider the health implications of economic policies and to take steps to mitigate the negative impact of economic downturns on vulnerable populations."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Author: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Prof Cyprian Mostert",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "/bmi/about/Pages/cyprian-mostert.aspx",
                  "target": "_self",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", Mental Health Economist, BMI",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Read full paper "
          },
          {
